-16. **The target allowlist (P4-31).** `--allowlist <file>` is required for every non-dry run. The file is git-ignored, must be a regular file with no group or other permission bit (mode 0600 or stricter) and is not followed through a symbolic link; one entry per line, `#` starts a comment, blank lines are ignored. An entry is a `ws://`, `wss://`, `http://` or `https://` URL (the last two for WebRTC signalling) or an E.164 number (ADR 0029), optionally followed by fields written `name=value` and separated by spaces (amended 2026-10-27, BL-299, BL-300): `bot_holds_telephony_credentials=true|false` (required for an entry used with a `twilio-media-stream/1` target, rule 6); `auth_token_env=<NAME>` (the name of an environment variable, `[A-Z_][A-Z0-9_]{0,63}`); `origin=<scheme://host[:port]>`. An unknown field, a repeated field or a malformed value refuses the file. Authentication: when `auth_token_env` is set, the token is read from that variable at step 6 with the other keys and sent only as an `Authorization: Bearer` header of the WebSocket handshake or the signalling request; it is never put in the path or a query, never logged, stored, printed or reported, and a missing or empty variable refuses the run before any socket. Only the variable name is recorded. The `Origin` header sent is the entry's `origin` field; without that field no `Origin` header is sent. The variable name (or none) and the origin (or none) are recorded as labels in `tracer.sim_profile/1` (ADR 0027). Tracer never writes a token into a path; a runner that expects a path token (`/ws/{token}`, `/ws-client/{token}`) or a `?token=` query is called only through the header form. Target and entry are compared exactly after one normalisation: the scheme and the host in lower case, the default port written out (80 or 443), the path kept byte for byte (no percent-decoding, an empty path written `/`); a URL with user information, a query or a fragment, or a host outside ASCII, is refused as an entry and as 